<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Beylik of the West</h1><p class="st-meta">1563 CE – 1831 CE (approx.) · capital Mascara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The western province of Ottoman Algiers, governed from Mazouna, Mascara and finally Oran, on the frontier with Spain and Morocco.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a> created the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in 1563, with its first seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazouna">Mazouna</a>. As the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> consolidated control over the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zayyanid-kingdom-of-tlemcen">Zayyanid Kingdom of Tlemcen</a>, the capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mascara-algeria">Mascara</a> around 1700, closer to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-oran">Spanish Oran</a>, which the beys sought to recapture.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The beys governed the plains and highlands of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> through makhzen tribes, collecting taxes in grain and livestock. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustapha-bouchelaghem">Mustapha Bouchelaghem</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a> in 1708, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> retook it in 1732. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-el-kebir">Mohammed el-Kebir</a> took possession of Oran in 1792, made it his capital and built mosques there.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> in 1830, the last bey, Hassan, surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a> to the French in January 1831. The western tribes soon rallied to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-abdelkader">Emirate of Abdelkader</a>, while the territory became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/beylik-of-the-west.jpg" alt="Beylik of the West" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Poudou99 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Les_provinces_de_la_R%C3%A9gence_d%27Alger.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1563 CE – 1831 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mascara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mustapha Bouchelaghem, Mohammed el-Kebir, Hassan Bey</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber, Ottoman Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Beylik of Oran, Beylik of Mascara</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1697&amp;focus=beylik-of-the-west" aria-label="Beylik of the West on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4683 898 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Beylik of the West lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5003 1154L5077 1108M5003 1154L5077 1108M5003 1154L5003 1154"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5077 1108h0M5077 1108h0M5003 1154h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5003 1154h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5003 1154h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mascara. <a href="/atlas?year=1697&amp;focus=beylik-of-the-west">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
